{"request": {"upstream": "cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine", "fork_owner": "LucaKro", "branch": "claude/sweet-maxwell-rrkf3u"}, "recording": {"recorder": {"version": "0.0.1.dev406+g41b6b17dd", "commit": "41b6b17dd59be5a7c2d3349442e6e53ecaea2b23"}, "answers": [{"transport": "rest pages", "address": "repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls?head=LucaKro:claude%2Fsweet-maxwell-rrkf3u&state=all&per_page=100", "variables": {}, "answer": [[{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pulls/1041", "id": 5414707927, "html_url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/1041", "number": 1041, "state": "open", "title": "Build every book on pull requests and fail it when a cell raises", "user": {"login": "LucaKro", "id": 90992250, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/LucaKro", "html_url": "https://github.com/LucaKro", "type": "User"}, "body": "## Why\n\n<!-- github-workflow:why:start -->\nEvery merge to main leaves the published documentation of all packages stale: the coraplex book fails on a missing `rclpy`, and the Pages deploy waits for every book. Pull requests never built the books, and a book whose cells raise still built successfully, so 16 pages have been publishing tracebacks without CI noticing.\n<!-- github-workflow:why:end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>What changes, how it is tested, and what breaks</summary>\n\n<!-- github-workflow:changes:start -->\n## What it changes\n\n**The coraplex book builds again.** Its parameter-mixin-map directive imports every coraplex action module, and `coraplex.robot_plans.actions.core.misc` imports `coraplex.perception`, which imports `rclpy`. The book now builds in the ROS container, as semantic_digital_twin's does. The giskardpy book moves there too: its Cartesian goals example loads the PR2 from `iai_pr2_description`.\n\n**A broken book fails the pull request.** `build_all_docs.yml` ran only on main, so the pull request that broke the coraplex book passed CI. It now builds every book for each non-draft pull request, without deploying. A new push to a pull request cancels the docs run for its previous commit; runs on main are still serialized and never cancelled.\n\n**A cell that raises fails the build.** jupyter-book only logs a warning for such a cell and still exits successfully. Every book now sets `execute.raise_on_error: true`. Turning it on found 16 pages whose published output was a traceback; they now run against the current API:\n\n- **krrood:** keyword-only calls (`Match.from_`, `Role.has_role`, `QueryGraph`, `ConditionAndBindings`, the `InferenceExplanation` queries, the verbalization pipeline, the example domain's dataclasses), a `Predicate` without its `_verbalization_fragment_`, and `RWXNode`, which `krrood.rustworkx_utils` no longer exports\n- **random_events and probabilistic_model:** `Event.plot` moved to `random_events.plotting.EventPlotter`, `Polytope.from_2d_points` became `from_points`, a missing plotly import, an assignment split across two lines\n- **cramph:** a `str` passed where `plot_gantt_chart` takes a `Path`\n\n**A random_events bug behind one of those pages.** `Event.fill_missing_variables` kept simple sets cached by an earlier read, so they lacked the filled variables and `probability` raised a `KeyError`. The fix clears the cache, and a new test proves it.\n\n## How it is tested\n\n- The new test fails without the fix and passes with it; `test/random_events_test` passes (109 tests), and so does `test/probabilistic_model_test` without the GUI tests, which need a display library the test machine lacked (1581 passed)\n- A throwaway book with a raising cell exits 0 without `raise_on_error` and 1 with it\n- krrood, random_events, probabilistic_model and cramph build from scratch with `raise_on_error: true`, with no failed notebook\n- Not run locally: the coraplex, giskardpy and semantic_digital_twin books, which need the ROS container. This pull request's docs run is their first check, and semantic_digital_twin's book may still hold a failing cell that the new setting exposes\n- actionlint reports nothing for the changed workflow\n\n## What breaks\n\nNothing in the public API. Every non-draft pull request now runs seven book builds.\n\nLabels: `bug-fix`\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01GKSxTgfmTdbn5sd9MMX6bV\n<!-- github-workflow:changes:end -->\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\nProposed from https://github.com/LucaKro/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/149\n\n<!-- github-workflow:copy 5cccb520d855c0ddf4bbfa4543f3714268b6cc1ab9f5ce4d7a5ea08c1f9757b6 -->\n", "created_at": "2026-11-20T14:09:13Z", "merged_at": null, "requested_reviewers": [{"login": "Tigul", "id": 6172348, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Tigul", "html_url": "https://github.com/Tigul", "type": "User"}, {"login": "sunava", "id": 33067562, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunava", "html_url": "https://github.com/sunava", "type": "User"}, {"login": "AbdelrhmanBassiouny", "id": 36744004, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/AbdelrhmanBassiouny", "html_url": "https://github.com/AbdelrhmanBassiouny", "type": "User"}, {"login": "maltehue", "id": 122607802, "url": "https://api.github.com/users/maltehue", "html_url": "https://github.com/maltehue", "type": "User"}], "labels": [{"id": 9749475231, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/labels/documentation", "name": "documentation", "color": "0075ca", "description": "Improvements or additions to documentation"}, {"id": 9818515928, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/labels/Giskard", "name": "Giskard", "color": "fbca04", "description": ""}, {"id": 9818517350, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/labels/semDT", "name": "semDT", "color": "0e8a16", "description": ""}, {"id": 9818518134, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/label